import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Multi-shot resume on the cranelift engine — landing note","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"handl/project/notes/multishot-resume-cranelift.md","filePath":"vendored/handl/project/notes/multishot-resume-cranelift.md"}`),a={name:`handl/project/notes/multishot-resume-cranelift.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="multi-shot-resume-on-the-cranelift-engine-—-landing-note" tabindex="-1">Multi-shot <code>resume</code> on the cranelift engine — landing note <a class="header-anchor" href="#multi-shot-resume-on-the-cranelift-engine-—-landing-note" aria-label="Permalink to “Multi-shot resume on the cranelift engine — landing note”">​</a></h1><h2 id="status" tabindex="-1">Status <a class="header-anchor" href="#status" aria-label="Permalink to “Status”">​</a></h2><p>Landed. <code>resume</code> (ADR-0158 replay-journal model) runs on all three eval engines: tree-walk (reference), bytecode (native replay) and cranelift (journal through the shared <code>handle_dyn</code> hook + the tree-walk arrow interpreter). Design: <code>design/multishot-resume.md</code>.</p><p>This note is the changeset manifest — the working tree is not a git checkout, so the file inventory below is the hand-off record.</p><h2 id="summary" tabindex="-1">Summary <a class="header-anchor" href="#summary" aria-label="Permalink to “Summary”">​</a></h2><p>A handler clause may take a second parameter — the resumption:</p><div class="language-hnl"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">hnl</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>handle perform(choose, [1, 2]) + 100 with {</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  choose: (opts, resume) ~&gt; [resume(opts[0]), resume(opts[1])]</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>-- → [101, 102]</span></span></code></pre></div><p><code>resume(x)</code> re-runs the handled body from the <code>handle</code> boundary under a replay journal seeded with <code>entries[..i] ++ [(op, x)]</code>; the body&#39;s completed value (through the <code>return</code> clause) is <code>resume</code>&#39;s result. No continuation capture: the journal is data, so <code>resume</code> is copyable.</p><h3 id="cranelift-specifics" tabindex="-1">Cranelift specifics <a class="header-anchor" href="#cranelift-specifics" aria-label="Permalink to “Cranelift specifics”">​</a></h3><ul><li><code>NativeOpCtx::run_delimited</code> override installs the journal when the frame has no <code>__acc__</code> slot and the handler has a ≥2-ary clause, drives the body, then runs the <code>IO</code>-former + carried-handler postlude.</li><li><code>perform</code> is intercepted at every dispatch seam (<code>call</code>, <code>flow</code>, <code>call_host</code>, and <code>arr &lt;op&gt;</code>) before one-shot <code>perform_dispatch</code>.</li><li><code>__resume__</code> values are intercepted in <code>apply_closure_value_opts</code>, including the single-<code>Arr</code> unpack a <code>call</code> performs on positional args.</li><li>Cranelift arrow values run in the tree-walk interpreter (<code>apply_value_treewalk</code>), so a <code>resume</code> inside a clause body is applied by the <em>tree-walk</em>. <code>native_ops</code> hosts an engine-neutral driver table (<code>register_resumption_driver</code> / <code>drive_shared_resumption</code>) that bridges the two; <code>ACTIVE_EVAL_CTX</code> (installed for the duration of a clause application) recovers <code>&amp;mut EvalCtx</code> on the cranelift side.</li><li>Compiled-codegen unwinding: <code>helper_v2_error_is_suspended</code> makes <code>compile_args_v2</code> and <code>Seq</code> stop evaluating after a suspension, so the journal cursor stays at the suspending op. <code>EvalCtx::set_error</code> never overwrites a <code>Suspended</code>, and the journal latches its first suspension as a second guard.</li><li>Lifecycle: <code>native_ops::ResumeTableScope</code> clears the shared driver table plus each engine&#39;s journal/suspension tables when the outermost eval on the thread returns (nested evals only bump a depth counter).</li></ul><h2 id="files-changed" tabindex="-1">Files changed <a class="header-anchor" href="#files-changed" aria-label="Permalink to “Files changed”">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>engine-exec/src/native_ops.rs</code></td><td><code>ResumptionDriver</code> + shared driver table, <code>ResumeTableScope</code> (+ eval depth), rec-region fixpoint propagates <code>Suspended</code> instead of swallowing it, style cleanups</td></tr><tr><td><code>engine-exec/src/{io,lib,pattern_match}.rs</code></td><td>clippy cleanups (no behaviour change)</td></tr><tr><td><code>engine-exec-cranelift/src/lib.rs</code></td><td>journal driver (<code>ResumeJournal</code>/<code>ResumeSuspension</code>/<code>drive_journal</code>/<code>resume_from</code>/<code>resume_suspension</code>), <code>run_delimited</code> override, perform/<code>arr</code> seams, <code>__resume__</code> seam, <code>ACTIVE_EVAL_CTX</code>, <code>set_error</code> guard, <code>helper_v2_error_is_suspended</code>, table scope, node-accurate diagnostics, 5 tests</td></tr><tr><td><code>engine-exec-cranelift/src/compile.rs</code></td><td>declare/register the new helper, suspension short-circuits in <code>compile_args_v2</code> and <code>Seq{axis:0}</code>, item allows</td></tr><tr><td><code>engine-exec-cranelift/src/standalone.rs</code></td><td>treat a staticlib older than the crate&#39;s newest source as missing (rebuild) — a new <code>helper_v2_*</code> otherwise fails at <code>cc</code> link time</td></tr><tr><td><code>engine-exec-cranelift/tests/standalone_bootstrap.rs</code></td><td>skip the <code>multishot_resume</code> corpus case (standalone has no <code>Language</code> for arrow application)</td></tr><tr><td><code>engine-exec-cranelift/tests/{object_compilation.rs,conformance/harness.rs}</code></td><td>clippy cleanups</td></tr><tr><td><code>engine-exec-tree-walk/src/lib.rs</code></td><td><code>__resume__</code> seam consults the shared driver table; table scope in <code>eval_ast_rc_tagged</code>; cleanups</td></tr><tr><td><code>engine-exec-bytecode/src/lib.rs</code></td><td>table scope in <code>eval_ast_rc_with_args</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>engine-exec-bytecode/src/vm.rs</code></td><td>3 resume tests (both continuations, nested cartesian, one-shot regression)</td></tr><tr><td><code>engine-exec-bytecode/src/compile.rs</code></td><td>clippy cleanups</td></tr><tr><td><code>host/crates/handl-test-utils/src/conformance/corpus.rs</code></td><td><code>multishot_resume</code> eval-corpus case — the cross-engine gate</td></tr><tr><td><code>host/crates/handl-runtime/tests/engine_parity.rs</code></td><td><code>perform_multishot_resume</code> (both continuations / nested / escape, all three engines); fixed the <code>vsum&lt;n&gt;</code> self-recursion case (<code>{n}</code> → <code>&lt;n&gt;</code>, the pre-existing failure was a test-source syntax bug) and extended it to tree-walk + cranelift with bytecode&#39;s known divergence pinned</td></tr><tr><td><code>host/project/adrs/0158-*.md</code>, <code>host/project/design/multishot-resume.md</code></td><td>status, deltas, limits</td></tr><tr><td><code>engine-parse-pratt/src/{lib,former_decl}.rs</code>, <code>host/crates/plugin-ext-typecheck/tests/scratch_ast_dump.rs</code></td><td>incidental clippy fixes (crate test suites re-run green)</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="verification" tabindex="-1">Verification <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification" aria-label="Permalink to “Verification”">​</a></h2><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>cargo test                 # engine-exec           13 passed</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>cargo test                 # engine-exec-cranelift 104 passed</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>cargo test                 # engine-exec-bytecode   94 passed</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>cargo test                 # engine-exec-tree-walk 142 passed</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>cargo test                 # host/crates/handl-runtime (engine_parity + rest)</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>cargo clippy --all-targets # all four engine crates: no warnings</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id="known-limits" tabindex="-1">Known limits <a class="header-anchor" href="#known-limits" aria-label="Permalink to “Known limits”">​</a></h2><p>See <code>design/multishot-resume.md</code> §&quot;Known limits&quot;: deterministic bodies only; <code>resume</code> escapes are supported while the eval is live, not across evals (the tables are reclaimed at the eval boundary); <code>perform</code> inside a <code>rec</code>/loop fixpoint region now propagates instead of being dropped but is still not a supported position; bytecode remains divergent on self-recursive closures (<code>vsum</code> → <code>Zero</code>, pinned in <code>engine_parity</code>).</p><h2 id="landing" tabindex="-1">Landing <a class="header-anchor" href="#landing" aria-label="Permalink to “Landing”">​</a></h2><p>No VCS in this working tree. To land, copy the files above into a clean checkout, or <code>git init</code> here and commit the tree as one change; the table in this note is the review manifest.</p>`,18)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};